From cf27a61e48a0772c170654f928b4ede04321367b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:26:46 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op local pads: split-screen players get Npads 2 to 4

oot-remake-multiplayer's patch 0016 (host only, no lift), on top of patch 0015. A pad the co-op module hands to a second, third or fourth player on this PC is left out of player 1's merged pad (and its motion and rumble) and answers the game's reads of Npad No.2 to No.4. Pads are named as patch 0015 names them, by their place in SDL's list; 0015's filter keeps a taken pad as this game's. host/pad_sdl.c keeps each pad's own state; host/nn_hid.c gives those Npads their style and states (no keyboard, script or Ocarina note keys; still while the Insert menu has the pads and after it until the pad is let go) and logs once which Npads the game supports. Three exports of the exe for the module, found by name: hos_coop_pad_info, hos_coop_pad_read and hos_coop_pad_take. Nothing changes until the module takes a pad.
